From 8cd1bc395cd520361613c0c7df0184829597b529 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:26:48 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] XHTTP: Count what the flow governor's client holds by
 connection as well as by stream

The send window counted the streams the server had not finished, so a
download it had ended and the client had not read was outside the limit.

What the client holds is now counted two ways and the larger taken: by
stream as before, and by what the client has not returned connection credit
for, taken as how far the connection window stands under the most it has
stood at. The connection's count is used only once the client has returned
connection credit in small steps.
